<%#
  This product's share of total historical demand, on the currently selected
  metric. The bar is scaled against the leader rather than against 100%.

  Used on the podium only. Demand here is extremely top-heavy -- the leading
  product is around half of all units, and nothing below rank 3 clears 3% -- so
  further down the page every bar is a 2px stub that says less than the
  percentage beside it. Rescaling per section would make them readable but would
  put two different scales on one page, which misleads more than it shows.

  locals: share (0.0..1.0), max_share
%>
<%
  scale = max_share.to_f.positive? ? max_share.to_f : 1.0
  width = [[(share / scale * 100).round, 100].min, 2].max
%>
<div class="flex items-center gap-x-3">
  <div class="h-1.5 flex-1 rounded-full bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-700 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="h-full rounded-full bg-red-500" style="width: <%= width %>%"></div>
  </div>
</div>
